Liquid Personnel is &nbsp;currently recruiting for an Occupational Therapist to join the&nbsp;West Locality Adult Social Care Team, supporting adults aged 18+ to live safely and independently within their communities.

This is a rewarding opportunity to use your OT expertise to complete person-centred assessments, promote independence and help prevent, reduce or delay the need for formal care and support.

What will your responsibilities be? &nbsp;

• Undertake person-centred Occupational Therapy assessments with adults aged 18+.

• Assess people's strengths, abilities and support needs to help them live safely in the community.

• Promote independence and maximise individuals' strengths and capabilities.

• Take a&nbsp;strengths-based approach&nbsp;to prevent, reduce or delay the need for care and support.

• Support carers to continue in their caring role for as long as they wish or are able to.

• Provide specialist OT advice and guidance to colleagues within the Adult Social Care team.

• Undertake supervisory responsibilities where directed by the Team Leader.

• Maintain accurate and robust records in line with&nbsp;HCPC and professional body requirements.

• Apply relevant legislation and professional guidance, including the&nbsp;Care Act 2014, Safeguarding, Mental Capacity, DoLS and CHC.

• Work collaboratively with colleagues and partner agencies to achieve positive outcomes for residents.

• Carry out visits to clients' homes, care homes and other community settings.

Benefits: &nbsp;

Know an Occupational Therapist who could be a great fit? Refer them to us and you could be eligible for a&nbsp;referral bonus if they successfully secure a placement. &nbsp;

Important: Driving &amp; Travel

A&nbsp;full driving licence and access to your own vehicle are essential&nbsp;for this position.

You’ll be required to undertake regular visits to clients' homes, care homes and other community settings, alongside working from the Market Street office.

Working Pattern

This is a&nbsp;hybrid role, with:

• 3 days per week in the Market Street office

• Community visits as required

• Regular travel to clients' homes, care homes and other relevant locations

Working Pattern: Hybrid - 3 days per week in the office, plus community visits

Qualifications &amp; Experience: &nbsp;

• Current registration as an Occupational Therapist.

• Experience working in Adult Social Care or a similar environment.

• The ability to work confidently in a community-based role, completing assessments and supporting adults to maximise their independence.

